---

# 19. LIVES

Each team begins with:

3 lives.

Represent compactly:

❤️ ❤️ ❤️

Incorrect challenge attempts may remove one life.

However:

DO NOT permanently eliminate teams.

When all lives are lost:

Apply configurable penalty.

Default:

60-second lockout.

Display:

RECOVERY MODE

"Your expedition needs time to recover."

00:60

After timer:

Restore one life and allow continuation.

Admin should be able to configure or disable this mechanic.

---

# 20. HINT SYSTEM

Each team receives:

2 hints by default.

Hints must be controlled by backend.

Example:

HINT AVAILABLE

Using a hint costs 200 points.

[USE HINT]

Confirmation:

USE ONE HINT?

Cost: -200 points

Hints should guide rather than reveal the exact answer.

Example ASCII challenge hint:

"Computers often map numbers to characters using a standard encoding."

Not:

"67 = C."

Admin should be able to configure hint text and hint cost.

---

# 21. SCORING ENGINE

Make scoring configurable.

Default:

Initial score:
1000

Level completion:
+500

Wrong answer:
-50

Hint:
-200

Final completion:
+1000

Optionally add time bonuses.

Never allow client-side score modification.

Backend calculates all scores.

Store score events so organizers can audit why a team has a particular score.

Example:

score_events

TEAM
EVENT
POINTS
TIMESTAMP

Byte Raiders
LEVEL_COMPLETE
+500

Byte Raiders
WRONG_ATTEMPT
-50

Byte Raiders
HINT_USED
-200

