# 38. UX DETAILS

When a player solves something correctly:

Do not instantly change screens.

Use sequence:

ANSWER ACCEPTED
↓
environment reacts
↓
clue revealed
↓
fragment discovered
↓
next location unlocked
↓
player chooses CONTINUE

This gives each solution emotional payoff.

Wrong answers should provide feedback without publicly humiliating players.

Use:

"SEQUENCE REJECTED"

rather than:

"WRONG!!!"

---

# 39. ACCESSIBILITY

Maintain sufficient contrast.

Do not communicate success/failure using color alone.

Keyboard navigation should work.

Code must be selectable.

Buttons require clear focus states.

Use semantic HTML where appropriate.

Respect reduced-motion settings.

